 "final_message": "I've made all twelve changes. The test suite passes, but I didn't write tests for most of the new behaviour (only the two you asked for), so those fixes are untested.\n\n- **Items 1\u20133, 6, 7 (`conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts`):** each now follows its SPEC section. Only a `converted` value of `True` counts as converted.\n- **Items 4\u20135 (`parse_session_log`):** `1`, `0` and empty now map to `True`, `False` and `None`. Blank lines, whitespace-only lines and `#` lines are skipped. A wrong field count or a non-integer `day` raises `ValueError` with `line N`.\n- **Item 8 (`campaign_summary`):** the rate is rounded to 3 decimals and `groups` counts only groups that have sessions.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added the two tests, one for `None` values in `conversion_rate` and one for duplicate ids in `dedupe_sessions`.\n- **Item 11:** the README's `conversions_in_window` entry is corrected, and `daily_conversion_counts` has a new entry.\n- **Item 12 (rest of the package):**\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` returns `None` for an empty group and sorts its keys.\n  - `longest_flag_streak` was never resetting its run count on a zero day, so I fixed that.\n\nOne thing the spec doesn't cover: a `converted` field that isn't `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise `ValueError` with `line N` for it, rather than guess a value. If you'd prefer it be treated as `None`, that's a one-line change.",
